description:
File: rust/lichen-core/src/loadng.rs lines 122-123, 376-378, 434-436

Doc comments say 'produced/verified by link layer' but there is no SECURITY: comment explaining:
1. What happens if link layer fails to verify (undefined behavior? caller's problem?)
2. Whether unsigned messages (signature=None) are valid on authenticated channels
3. The trust boundary between this codec and the link layer

Per project standards, security-critical code paths must have SECURITY: prefix comments.

Fix: Add SECURITY: comments documenting the signature verification contract. Example:
// SECURITY: This codec only serializes signatures. Callers MUST verify
// signatures at the link layer before acting on message contents. Accepting
// signature=None on an authenticated channel is a vulnerability.
